/*****************************************************************************
    scopeProbe -- CONTAINMENT MEASUREMENT for the define-time name-search
    escape (Clay relay, "define-time name search escapes scope", 2026-08-01).

    RECON ONLY. No fix. Nothing here mutates shared state: every name this file
    introduces was grepped unique first, every registry is minted here, and the
    writes it demonstrates land in this process only.

    THE REPORTED FINDING, restated so this file stands alone: defining
        testForC argument second=56 third="WTF?"          (incant/unitTests:153)
    writes 56 and "WTF?" into `sample`'s OWN `second` and `third`
    (incant/unitTests:96-104) instead of minting fresh attributes on testForC.

    ⚠ ATTRIBUTION IS SINGLE-VARIABLE, and it is not measured here -- it is
    measured by A/B against `incant/scopeUnits`, a copy of unitTests differing
    in EXACTLY ONE LINE (testForC's two attributes removed). Run both and walk
    sample:
        with    testForC argument second=56 third="WTF?"  ->  second 56 / third WTF?
        without                                            ->  second second / third third
    That is the whole attribution. See docs/nameScopeRecon.md for the driver.

    WHAT *THIS* FILE MEASURES -- how far the escape reaches, which is the
    question that decides whether a fence can contain it:

      row 1  is the colliding name reachable as a BARE name at all?
             (i.e. is it on locate()'s walk, or only a member of sample?)
      row 2  a DIFFERENT registry AND a DIFFERENT file -- still leaks?
      row 3  a PLAIN GROUP definition, no `argument`, no `code={}` --
             is this specific to action-attribute syntax?

    Row 2 is the discriminating one. locate() walks currentRegistry FIRST and
    then every registry on the searchList in order, so if the escape follows the
    search list then a registry fence alone cannot contain it -- which is the
    difference between "scope the definition" and "scope the lookup".

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT (CLAUDE.md third corollary). This file's first draft
    died exactly the way that corollary describes: a stray bare top-level
    statement (bear-trap #15) truncated the run, and it still exited 0. The
    missing sentinel is what said so.
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);

search reset stack Grokking;
search UnitTests list;

register(ScopeC);
define
    actQQ argument fourth=77 code={ };
    ;

register(ScopeD);
define
    hostQ fifth=88;
    ;

register(ScopeProbe);
define
    walkSample code={
        iterate spIter on sample;
        while ++spIter;
            print + `taG spIter:;
        };
    ;

print "1 is the colliding name on locate()'s walk? (bare-name reach)";
print + "bare second =" second:;
print + "bare fourth =" fourth:;
print + "bare fifth  =" fifth:;
print "2+3 sample's list AFTER two foreign definitions:";
print + "  actQQ argument fourth=77   -- other registry, other file, an ACTION";
print + "  hostQ fifth=88             -- other registry, other file, a PLAIN GROUP";
walkSample();
print "SP SENTINEL":;
stop();
